## Scope

If an aggregation endpoint is justified, let users explicitly contribute the
automatic compatibility result. This is crowdtesting of execution compatibility,
not retrieval relevance.

## Exit criteria

- Default behavior sends nothing.
- The opt-in payload contains only pass/fail, exact entry fingerprint and the
  minimum runtime/provider/platform shape needed to group failures.
- Tests prove library text, query text, vectors and Zotero identifiers cannot
  enter the payload.
- Aggregate presentation states compatibility and sample size, never a quality
  ranking or automatic default.
